Services [Worker]
To open a list, into which you type the names of the services, which the Worker provides, click this button.
Remarks
Before you can type in data, click the Inheritance check box so that it looks like this 
 .
• The Worker provides these services by default:
• Type the name of the service into the cell and click Apply. The Worker attempts to provide the services
in the order in which you type them into the list. You might, for example, enter repair, drilling,
milling, turning, carrying parts, etc.
Note
The name is not case-sensitive, just like the names of attributes and methods of the objects are not
case-sensitive.
To save memory and improve access speed, all places which are using such a case-insensitive string
are pointing to the same string in main memory. The visible and unexpected result is that the first
occurrence of the string defines how the string is written in terms of upper- and lower-casing.
In SimTalk you can compare strings in an case-insensitive manner with the ~= operator, compare
Relational Operators.
If you type in a Priority and an Efficiency for each individual service, Plant Simulation uses these values.
By typing in a Priority and an Efficiency, you are better able to control the automatic assignment of the
services, which the Worker provides for jobs to be done.
Services [Worker]
Plant Simulation Help 11-3165
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

If you do not type in a Priority and an Efficiency for an individual service, Plant Simulation uses the
values for the Priority and the Efficiency of the Worker.
Plant Simulation inserts these services into the list of offered services of the Broker: To view them, select
View > Offered Services.
You can use the commands on the Context Menu of Embedded Lists to edit the contents of the cells.
If you want the Worker to provide additional services, you can type in these services into the Workers to
Create table.
