Tab Scope
Assign any of the built-in material flow objects, or a Frame, to which the Worker can be brokered to
perform a job, on the tab Scope.
Remarks
To add an object to the scope of the Worker to the tab Scope, drag it from the Frame window over the icon
of the Worker class and drop it there. You can also select and then drag-and-drop multiple objects at the
same time!
Note
Plant Simulation always resolves relative paths in relation to the Frame in which the WorkerPool is
inserted. If Plant Simulation cannot resolve a path in the Scope array during the simulation, it shows an
error message and asks if you would like to stop the simulation.
To manipulate the contents of the list, use the commands on the Context Menu of Embedded Lists.
You can also enter the Scope into the Workers to Create table.
